From: NixOS Android devices contributors <nixos-android-devices@localhost>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 22:50:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: preserve encoded SM8450 UniPro divider

Local correction to the SM8475 boot dependency patch. Frequency table
and RCGR layout follow Linux gcc-sm8450.c:
https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v7.3-rc4/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8450.c

F() encodes divider 2 as HID=3. clk_rcg_set_rate() encodes this again
as HID=5 and ORs it into the old divider. For old CFG=0x103 this yields
0x107, which is 150 MHz, while ufs-qcom sets timers for 300 MHz.
Asphalt runtime reads confirm CFG=0x107 and the 600 MHz GPLL0 parent.
Replace divider/source/mode bits explicitly, using the encoded value.
Only the SM8450 UniPro clock changes; retain existing PLL programming.
---
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/clock-sm8450.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/clock-sm8450.c
@@ -1,3 +1,8 @@
 		freq = qcom_find_freq(ftbl_ufs, rate);
-		clk_rcg_set_rate(priv->base, 0x8708c, freq->pre_div, freq->src);
+		/* F() already encodes the HID divider; replace the old divider. */
+		clrsetbits_le32(priv->base + 0x87090,
+			       GENMASK(4, 0) | GENMASK(10, 8) |
+			       GENMASK(13, 12) | BIT(20),
+			       freq->pre_div | freq->src);
+		clk_bcr_update(priv->base + 0x8708c);
 		return freq->freq;
